  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from the Fetch Standard Body mixin (Request/Response) and W3C FileAPI (Blob): the feature adds exactly one method on three interfaces, with no dictionaries, enums, events, or options. Independent-review corrections reflected: null-body lifecycle (bodyUsed stays false; repeated calls return distinct closed streams \u2014 consumption/single-use applies only to non-null bodies, per WPT null-body tests); the exact five FileAPI failure reasons (NotFound, UnsafeFile, TooManyReads, SnapshotState, FileLock) with the raw stream failure reason distinguished from FileReader DOMException mappings; vendor signals cited from the ChromeStatus API record (Safari 'Positive' is a recorded signal, not an official WebKit standards position) with BCD support rows kept separate and extended (Node.js 26.5.0, Android/WebView mirrors, Deno unknown); visible chrome-platform-showcase source label linked; TextDecoderOptions.fatal claims cite the definition anchor."
